<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Maritime Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Tabanan</h1><p class="st-meta">1600 CE – 1906 CE (approx.) · capital Tabanan</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Rice-rich kingdom of south-western Bali whose ruling house ended in tragedy during the Dutch conquest of 1906.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Tabanan traced its ruling dynasty to Arya Kenceng, a noble said to have come to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bali">Bali</a> with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majapahit-empire">Majapahit</a> conquest of the 14th century. The house became an independent kingdom as the central <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-gelgel">Gelgel</a> state broke apart in the 17th century, ruling the fertile slopes between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-batukaru">Mount Batukaru</a> and the south coast.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The kings, styled Cokorda, ruled through branches of the royal family and allied noble houses, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmins">Brahmana</a> priests serving the court. The economy rested on wet-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> farming organised by subak irrigation societies, and Tabanan became one of the granaries of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bali">Bali</a>. Its courts were active patrons of temple festivals and gamelan.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1906, after the puputan of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-badung">Kingdom of Badung</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> troops advanced on Tabanan. The raja <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gusti-ngurah-agung">Gusti Ngurah Agung</a> surrendered and took his own life in captivity with his son. The kingdom was annexed into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/dutch-east-indies">Dutch East Indies</a>, though the royal house remains locally prominent.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1600 CE – 1906 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r